<article class="env-lemma" id="0AE6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AE6">Lemma <span data-tag="0AE6">88.30.4</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $f : X \to S$ be an object of (<a href="/tag/0AS2" data-tag="0AS2">88.30.0.1</a>) such that $f$ is proper. Then there exists a $U$-admissible blowup $S' \to S$ which dominates $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Special case of More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/087G" data-tag="087G">76.39.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>